#!/usr/bin/python3
# AllRice monitor on M1 and its watchdog on huihuimac (MET-222; rules: AGENTS.md at the
# repository root; how to run and drill it: docs/runbooks/m1-monitor.md). Python 3.9
# standard library only: launchd starts it with /usr/bin/python3 and an empty PATH.
#
#   monitor run [--config <file>]                   one round of checks (launchd: every 5 minutes)
#   monitor peer [--config <file>]                  huihuimac side: is M1 alive, is it reachable from outside
#   monitor status [--config <file>]                open alerts, last round, delivery backlog
#   monitor test-alert [--config <file>]            send one test message
#   monitor launchd install|remove [--peer] [--config <file>]
#   monitor ingest-incidents [--config <file>]      write incidents the peer sends on stdin (over SSH)
#
# Every check returns findings keyed by what it watches. A key that turns bad opens an
# alert; while it stays bad only an escalation or a reminder (hourly when critical) goes
# out; when it is good again "已恢复" goes out. A key that keeps flapping is muted for an
# hour after one notice. All changes of a round go out as one Telegram message and are
# written to allrice_operational_incidents. A failing component check is re-run once
# before it alerts, so a blip does not page. Each round ends by writing heartbeat.json,
# which the other machine reads over SSH: whichever side stops, the other one says so.
